# Worker Boundary Rule

Worker and multi-robot work must stay in Cursor-controlled branches.

Allowed worker areas:

- `automation/**`
- `automation/worker-runtime/**`
- `docs/automation/**`
- worker tests
- driver SDK
- job queue contracts
- checkpoint logic
- output persistence
- safety gates

Forbidden without explicit approval:

- Real bot execution
- Production scraping
- Production messaging
- Direct production database access from test code
- Unsafe UI trigger for worker execution
- Lovable edits to worker runtime

Lovable may only display worker status if an approved API contract already exists.

Cursor must not expose unsafe worker execution to UI without a reviewed API and safety gate.
